      "result": {
        "reply_text": "I understand that you paid for a washing machine repair service, but the leak persists and the company is no longer responding to your attempts to contact them.\n\nUnder the law, a product service provider can be held liable if the service they provided was faulty, deficient, or did not meet the terms of your contract. You have the right to bring a product liability action against a service provider for harm caused by their deficient service.\n\nYou may file a complaint with the District Consumer Commission. You can also try lodging a grievance through the National Consumer Helpline via their web portal, phone number, or messaging services. When doing so, you will need to provide details such as the company name, transaction date, amount paid, and your service bill.\n\nKeep your service bill and any records of your attempts to contact the company in a safe place. These will be important if you decide to file a formal complaint.\n\nYou should consider speaking with a lawyer if you need help drafting a formal complaint or if the company continues to ignore your requests for a resolution.\n\nCould you please provide the name of the repair service company and the specific date when the repair was performed?\n\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 83\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 85\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 82\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 35\nSource: National Consumer Helpline Grievance Redressal Procedure, procedure 1\n\nWhat I could not verify:\n- The provided sources do not explicitly state that video evidence is a required or accepted document proof for the National Consumer Helpline.\n\nThis is legal information, not legal advice.",
